# This repo is Python; it has no .nvmrc and runs no Node. The README documents
# the node rules using real tokens (`node:22.23.1`, `Node.js 22`), which is
# enough for `has_pins` to conclude the language is in use and report it as
# unchecked on every commit. Any document explaining these rules is the first
# thing to trip them.
README.md

# The toolchain definitions cite the token shapes their rules match
# (`nodejs22.x`, `pnpm@9.15.9`) as illustrations. Same reason .python-version-ignore
# excludes this directory: a rule's own documentation is the first thing it trips.
src/version_drift/toolchains/*
